  "final": "`notes export --format md|json|csv` now works, and all 21 tests pass. `md` is the default format.\n\n**What I built**\n- **Exporters:** three subagents wrote them in parallel. They are `notes/export/md.py`, `jsonfmt.py` and `csvfmt.py`, each with its own test file. I wired `notes/export/__init__.py` and `notes/cli.py` myself, and added `tests/test_export_cli.py`.\n- **Markdown format:** one `## title` section per note, with an `id / created / tags` line and then the body.\n- **JSON format:** an array of note objects, indented.\n- **CSV format:** header `id,title,body,tags,created`, with tags joined by `;`.\n- **README:** I added an Export section and updated the layout list.\n\n**Review of the integrated result**\n- I read all three exporters and ran each format from the CLI against a note with commas, quotes, a newline and tags. They came out correct, and the CSV quoted the awkward fields properly.\n- Output ends with exactly one newline, because the CLI adds one only when the exporter's text lacks it.\n- An unknown format is rejected by argparse.\n\nI used the cheaper haiku model for the exporter subagents. I didn't commit anything, and there are untracked `__pycache__` directories because the repo has no `.gitignore`.",
